{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JER",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JER.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said the LORD to me, Though Moses and Samuel stood before me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my mind ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "could",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards this people: cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of my sight, and let them go forth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass, if they say to thee, Whither shall we go forth? then thou shalt tell them, Thus saith the LORD; Such as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for death, to death; and such as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the sword, to the sword; and such as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the famine, to the famine; and such as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the captivity, to the captivity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will appoint over them four kinds, saith the LORD: the sword to slay, and the dogs to tear, and the fowls of the heaven, and the beasts of the earth, to devour and destroy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will cause them to be removed into all kingdoms of the earth, because of Manasseh the son of Hezekiah king of Judah, for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which he did in Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For who shall have pity upon thee, O Jerusalem? or who shall bemoan thee? or who shall go aside to ask concerning thy welfare?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast forsaken me, saith the LORD, thou art gone backward: therefore will I stretch out my hand against thee, and destroy thee; I am weary with repenting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will fan them with a fan in the gates of the land; I will bereave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of children, I will destroy my people, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "since",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they return not from their ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their widows are multiplied to me above the sand of the seas: I have brought upon them against the mother of the young men a spoiler at noon-day: I have caused ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to fall upon it suddenly, and terrors upon the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She that hath borne seven languisheth: she hath resigned her breath; her sun is gone down while ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet day: she hath been ashamed and confounded: and the residue of them will I deliver to the sword before their enemies, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe is me, my mother, that thou hast borne me a man of strife and a man of contention to the whole earth! I have neither lent on usury, nor have men lent to me on usury; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every one of them doth curse me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD said, Verily it shall be well with thy remnant; verily I will cause the enemy to treat thee ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "well",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the time of evil and in the time of affliction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall iron break the northern iron and the steel?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy substance and thy treasures will I give to the spoil without price, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for all thy sins, even in all thy borders.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to pass with thy enemies into a land ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou knowest not: for a fire is kindled in my anger, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall burn upon you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, thou knowest: remember me, and visit me, and avenge me of my persecutors; take me not away in thy long-suffering: know that for thy sake I have suffered rebuke.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy words were found, and I did eat them; and thy word was to me the joy and rejoicing of my heart: for I am called by thy name, O LORD God of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I sat not in the assembly of the mockers, nor rejoiced; I sat alone because of thy hand: for thou hast filled me with indignation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why is my pain perpetual, and my wound incurable, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " refuseth to be healed? wilt thou be altogether to me as a liar, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " waters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fail?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the LORD, If thou shalt return, then will I bring thee again, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou shalt stand before me: and if thou shalt separate the precious from the vile, thou shalt be as my mouth: let them return to thee; but return not thou to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will make thee to this people a fortified brazen wall: and they shall fight against thee, but they shall not prevail against thee: for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee to save thee and to deliver thee, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will deliver thee from the hand of the wicked, and I will redeem thee from the hand of the terrible.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
